.TH SHIP 1 "October 2026" "ship 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ship \- put an HTML page on one of your Cloudflare domains
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ship
.I file.html
.RI [ target ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B ship
.I folder/
.RI [ target ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B ship ls
.br
.B ship rm
.I target
.RB [ \-y ]
.br
.B ship setup
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ship
takes an HTML file (or a folder) from your computer and puts it online at
a domain you own. It uploads the files, connects the domain, and waits
until the page answers. Then it prints the link and copies it to your
clipboard.
.PP
Running the same command again replaces the page. The link stays the same.
.SH TARGETS
The
.I target
says where the page goes. It can be:
.TP
.B demo.example.com
A whole hostname. The page is at https://demo.example.com/
.TP
.B example.com/reports/q3
A path on a hostname. The page is at https://example.com/reports/q3/
.TP
.I (nothing)
A random, hard-to-guess link on your default hostname (chosen during
.BR "ship setup" ),
named after the file. For example, https://p.example.com/q3-report-8f3a1c/
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "ship " "file.html target"
Publish one HTML file. It is renamed to index.html. Images, CSS and other
files it links to are uploaded too, if they sit in the same folder or
below it. Files elsewhere, like
.IR ../logo.png ,
are skipped with a warning.
.TP
.BI "ship " "folder/ target"
Publish a whole folder. It needs an
.I index.html
at the top. Hidden files such as
.I .DS_Store
and
.I .git
are skipped.
.TP
.B ship ls
List everything you have published, newest first.
.TP
.BI "ship rm " target
Delete a page. If the target is a whole hostname, the hostname is also
disconnected and its DNS record removed. Asks before deleting.
.TP
.B ship setup
Save your Cloudflare API token and prepare the account (storage bucket
and Worker). Run it once at the start, and again whenever you get a new
token. It is safe to run any number of times.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-force
Publish even if the hostname already points somewhere else. This
.B deletes
the hostname's existing DNS records. Without it,
.B ship
refuses, so you can't break a real website by mistake.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
With
.BR "ship rm" :
don't ask for confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help for
.B ship
or for any command, e.g.
.BR "ship rm \-\-help" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Put a page online at a random link:
.PP
.RS
ship report.html
.RE
.PP
Put it at a hostname of your choice:
.PP
.RS
ship report.html demo.example.com
.RE
.PP
Put it under a path:
.PP
.RS
ship report.html example.com/reports/q3
.RE
.PP
A file name with spaces needs quotes:
.PP
.RS
ship "Q3 Report.html" demo.example.com
.RE
.PP
Publish a folder of HTML, images and CSS:
.PP
.RS
ship ./my-site/ app.example.com
.RE
.PP
Update a page: run the same command again.
.PP
See what's online, then take one page down:
.PP
.RS
ship ls
.br
ship rm demo.example.com
.RE
.SH TOKEN EXPIRY
Your Cloudflare token has an expiry date.
.B ship
starts warning you 14 days before it, and stops working once it has passed.
To renew:
.IP 1. 4
Go to https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens and either
.B Roll
the old token (same permissions, new value) or create a new one with the
same permissions.
.IP 2. 4
Run
.BR "ship setup" ,
answer
.B n
when asked whether to use the saved token, and paste the new one.
.PP
Your published pages stay online the whole time. An expired token only
stops you from publishing.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.TP
.B "Uploaded, but not answering yet"
A brand-new hostname can take a few minutes to get its DNS record and
HTTPS certificate. Check whether Cloudflare has the record:
.RS
.PP
dig +short demo.example.com @1.1.1.1
.PP
If that shows addresses but the page doesn't load on your computer, your
network cached an old "doesn't exist" answer. Try your phone on mobile
data, or wait up to 30 minutes.
.RE
.TP
.B "already has DNS records"
The hostname is already in use. Pick another, or use
.B \-\-force
if you really want to replace what's there.
.TP
.B "token may have expired"
See TOKEN EXPIRY above.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ship/config.json
Settings: account, default hostname, bucket and Worker names.
.TP
.I macOS Keychain, entry \(dqship\(dq
Your Cloudflare API token.
.TP
.B SHIP_CLOUDFLARE_TOKEN
Environment variable. If set, it is used instead of the Keychain token.
.SH HOW IT WORKS
Every page is stored in one Cloudflare R2 bucket
.RI ( ship\-sites ),
in a folder named after its hostname. One Cloudflare Worker
.RI ( ship\-router )
serves all of them: it reads the hostname and path of each visit and
returns the matching file. Publishing to a new hostname connects it to the
Worker. Cloudflare then creates the DNS record and HTTPS certificate on
its own.
.PP
Pages are public to anyone with the link, and they tell search engines
not to index them.
.SH SOURCE
https://github.com/JoseUlisesQuevedo/ship
